[38;5;231m⏺[39m Section 3 of 3 — [1mtesting, and the tooling question.[0m

  The repo has nothing to build on: no [38;5;153mscripts[39m block, no dependencies, no test runner, no linter, no tests anywhere. So
  this is a from-scratch choice, and it's cheapest to make now, before the code exists.

  What I'd test, given the design:

  - [38;5;153mrules.js[39m — each factory's [38;5;153mtest[39m in isolation, including the boundaries that bite: [38;5;153mrequired()[39m against [38;5;153m""[39m, [38;5;153m"   "[39m, and
    [38;5;153mundefined[39m; [38;5;153mminLength[39m exactly at n; [38;5;153memail()[39m against a few things that look valid but aren't; [38;5;153mmatches()[39m when the
    referenced field is absent from [38;5;153mallValues[39m.
  - [38;5;153mvalidate.js[39m — a field stopping at its first failing rule while other fields still report; the empty-[38;5;153merrors[39m shape
    when valid; a schema field missing from [38;5;153mvalues[39m.
  - [38;5;153mbind.js[39m — this is the part that needs a DOM. Node 22 has no [38;5;153mdocument[39m, so either these tests run under jsdom, or
    [38;5;153mbindForm[39m gets tested through a small hand-rolled fake element. I'd rather add jsdom as the one devDependency than
    invent a fake DOM, but it is a dependency in a repo that currently has zero.

  Since [38;5;153mrules.js[39m and [38;5;153mvalidate.js[39m are deliberately DOM-free, the majority of the suite runs on [38;5;153mnode:test[39m with no
  dependencies at all — that's the payoff for keeping the engine pure.

  For the runner I'd use Node's built-in [38;5;153mnode:test[39m plus [38;5;153mnode:assert[39m: zero install, and it imports ES modules natively.
  Jest or Vitest would both mean pulling in a toolchain this project has no other use for.

  On the assumption in section 1 — building the signup form — its real test is that it needs no changes to [38;5;153mrules.js[39m or
  [38;5;153mvalidate.js[39m. If it does, the abstraction is wrong and I'd rather find that out now than call the task done.

